{
 "version": 1,
 "name": "tavern",
 "archetype": "building.tavern",
 "description": "A medieval timber-framed inn with its door on the +Z front: a stone ground floor with dressed quoins and a plinth, one or two jettied upper storeys on projecting joists with a bressumer, dark posts, rails, braces and plates over plastered infill, glowing leaded windows, timbered gable ends with a king post, a steep tiled or thatched roof with a ridge roll and barge boards, a brick chimney with pots, a plank door hinged at its side with iron straps and a ring pull, a gabled porch on posts, a hanging sign on an iron bracket that swings about x, and a barrel by the door.",
